sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant M as macOS Controller
    participant N as LAN / TLS
    participant W as Windows Agent

    U->>M: Select discovered Windows device
    M->>W: Pair request (authenticated transport bootstrap)
    W->>U: Show pairing approval on Windows
    U->>W: Approve
    W-->>M: Pair confirmation / peer identity
    M->>W: Verify identity and establish trusted session
    W-->>M: Session ready + capabilities
    M-->>U: Connected status

    U->>M: Move pointer to configured edge
    M->>M: Change active input target
    M->>N: Input events (validated, sequenced)
    N->>W: Forward input events
    W->>W: Validate session and inject supported input
    W-->>M: Input acknowledgement / status

    U->>M: Emergency shortcut or connection loss
    M->>M: Stop forwarding; restore local input
    M->>N: End session / release-all if possible
    N->>W: Session end
    M-->>U: Local control restored
